## Conclusion and limits

Over 10^3 to 10^7 the mean absolute error falls as N^−0.50, consistent with the Monte Carlo rate N^−1/2, and the measured values agree with the theoretical amplitude 1.31/√N to within about 2 standard errors at every N (largest at N = 10^4, +1.74 SE). With five sizes and 200 runs each, this shows consistency with −1/2 and not proof of the exact exponent; the interval reflects finite-run sampling noise only, not model discrepancy.
